# Build context hygiene.
#
# The Go image and the inference image both build from the repository root, so
# this file applies to both: it can exclude what neither needs, and nothing
# either one does. `ml/` and `web/` stay, because the inference image copies
# `ml/` and excluding it fails the build with a confusing "not found".
#
# What is excluded is what would be expensive or wrong to ship: the dataset is
# hundreds of megabytes and is licensed for individual use, the models are
# mounted at runtime rather than baked in, and the virtualenv and node_modules
# are built inside the images from their lockfiles.
.git
.github
.idea
data
models
docs
.venv
**/node_modules
web/dist
*.parquet
*.ndjson
*.csv
